            <ArticleTitle>[Clinico-genealogical characteristics of patients with ischemic heart disease and different disorders of lipid metabolism].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>13-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The paper presents a clinical and genealogical characterization of 50 probands suffering from coronary heart disease concurrent with various lipid metabolic disturbances and 211 first-degree relatives whose data have been obtained from the probands' histories while making up their pedigrees. The prevalence of atherosclerosis among the first-degree relatives has been demonstrated to be related to the nature of lipid metabolic disturbances in a proband. Some dyslipoproteinemias in the proband have been characterized by early onset of coronary heart disease, stroke, and their grave course in close relatives.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
